  body: "# Child Benefit evidence for Widowed Mother’s Allowance\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\nThe WMA guidance
    distinguishes the dependent Child Benefit entitlement question, decided by HMRC, from the DM’s WMA decision,
    and directs the DM to seek evidence from HMRC.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\nThe source expressly excepts pregnancy
    cases from this dependency. A later Child Benefit decision can establish entitlement from before death. These
    statements are scoped to legacy WMA and are not copied into every bereavement benefit.\n\n## Inspected passages\n\
    \n- [DMG 58202, PDF page 7](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a8050b9ed915d74e33f9b7e/dmgch58.pdf#page=7).\n\
    - [DMG 58203, PDF page 7](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a8050b9ed915d74e33f9b7e/dmgch58.pdf#page=7).\n\
    \n## Evidence and review status\n\nIndependent experimental interpretation of captured DWP guidance, not an
    official DWP document. Definitions and semantic associations are model-assisted proposals awaiting specialist
    review. No individual entitlement decision, medical conclusion, award calculation or executable rule is provided.\n\
    \nSource observation, listing-page update, printed revision, legal event and claimant-event dates are separate.
    Current legal applicability is unresolved. Page numbers are one-based PDF positions; machine extraction may
    damage reading order, characters and footnotes. No visual PDF or specialist acceptance is claimed.\n\n- `dmg-vol10-ch58`:
    PDF `6b9d46772e961138cd132e6441896d15c2c5f90f76d2577f72119654be82d3f8`; extracted pages `6d6ef555ba93c68a3a178d5cc02057ef4b54ad3dba4b14baa5c18491c307c94c`;
    acquired `2026-09-15T19:45:32.573488Z`.\n"
  resource: https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a8050b9ed915d74e33f9b7e/dmgch58.pdf#page=7
